    <div class="row">
        <div class="span12">
            <h3 class="headline">
                <span>Desktop Automation (Early BETA)</span>
            </h3>
        </div>
        <div class="span12">

         
            <p>BETA PAGE - UNDER CONSTRUCTION - The DesktopAutomation XModule is a native app for Windows, Mac and Linux.
            It directly interacts with the operating system to allow <em>Ui.Vision RPA</em> to run computer vision directly on the desktop. Together with 
            Kantu's RealUser Simulation XModule, this takes desktop automation to a new level and makes <em>Ui.Vision RPA</em> the most powerful tool for cross-platform
            desktop automation.
             </p>
            <p>The DesktopAutomation XModule adds only one new commands: XDesktopAutomation | true/false</p>

            <p>What this command does is to switch the <em>Ui.Vision RPA</em> eyes from the browser to the desktop. So now XClick (image) or XClick (ocr=text) operate on the desktop, and
            can automate anything that a human can automate.</p>

            <p>How to create desktop automation macros:</p>

            <p>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        <i class="fa fa-hdd-o"></i> Note that the "Recording" mode is only for Selenium IDE type macros. It does not work with XClick.
                    </li></br>
                    <li>
                        <i class="fa fa-hdd-o"></i> XClick macros are best constructed like a Lego car: Add each XClick command to the macro, and build the macro step by step.
                    </li></br>
                    <li>
                        <i class="fa fa-hdd-o"></i> In the <em>Ui.Vision RPA</em> settings, on the new VISION tab, select "Desktop Automation" as operating mode. Then the "Select" and "Find" buttons
                    operate on the desktop.
                    </li></
                </ul>

            </p>

           <p>Desktop Automation is in an early beta stage - please report issues in the forum. Known issues: XMove and Relative Clicks are not yet supported.</p>
